## AFTER Auto-LF — arm immediately (all paths)

Arm starts right after Auto-LF succeeds — **never** wait for PR to arm.

| Case outcome | Close-out command (background) | Finishing quote |
|---|---|---|
| **EMAIL non-transfer** | **`--closeout-anwenden`** immediately after Auto-LF | `LF done for #FALL_ID — armed, awaiting PR or Anwenden.` |
| **EMAIL transfer** | **`--closeout-weiter`** or **`--closeout-extern`** | `LF TR done for #FALL_ID` |
| **CALL non-transfer** | **`--closeout-next`** | `LF done for #FALL_ID` |
| **CALL transfer** | **`--closeout-weiter`** / **`--closeout-extern`** | `LF TR done for #FALL_ID` |

**PR (EMAIL non-transfer):** Just pastes the reply — arm is already running. No new arm on PR. Finishing quote: `PR done for #FALL_ID`.

Do **not** arm Anwenden at PR time. Do **not** wait for PR before arming.

Do **not** arm Anwenden at Auto-LF time for EMAIL non-transfer — wait for **PR**.  
Do **not** wait for typed `LF` before arming transfer / CALL paths.

**Call listen:** Parked (`enabled=false`). Do not arm/prime call_listen on LF.

Full transfer UI click paths: `.cursor/rules/lf-tr-transfer.mdc`.  
Arm / await detail: `.cursor/rules/re-read-email.mdc`.

VIOLATION OF ONE-CASE RULE = DATA BREACH. DO NOT PROCEED IF UNCERTAIN.
